  "arc": "Fists up at chest height, elbows tucked, weight on the character-right foot. Frames 0-5 are a bounce, not a step: heels stay lifted, the drive is in the knees, and the weight rocks character-right to character-left.\n\nFrame 6 is the hinge \u2014 the fists drop onto the hips and the engine moves from arms to pelvis. The bounce carries to the end with the accent in the hips and the shoulders level. At 6 fps every cell is a held position rather than a passing one, so draw them as poses, not as blur.\n\nFrame 12 does not meet frame 0: the arms are on the hips at the end and up at the chest at the start (3.82x). The sheet plays out and back, which hides it there, but a straight loop shows the jump \u2014 blend the arms up across the last two frames.",
